  "summary": "This slice finishes Chapter 13’s survey of Vim enhancements (HTML conversion, vimdiff, viminfo and :mksession, long-line display, abbreviations, and quick tricks) and works through Chapter 14’s power techniques: convenience mappings, the command-line and search-history windows, awk-based buffer filtering and word-frequency analysis, and an enhanced status line. It then covers Vim as an IDE (plug-in managers, NERDTree, Fugitive, completion, Termdebug), vi’s presence in shells, screen, browsers, Word, and other tools, the epilogue, and the opening of Appendix A’s vi/ex command reference.",
